window.docContents[109].resolve({"/Lists/#Logical-Foundations--Lists___-Working-with-Structured-Data--Partial-Maps":{"contents":"As a final illustration of how data structures can be defined in\nLean, here is a simple partial map data type, analogous to the\nmap or dictionary data structures found in most programming\nlanguages.\n\nFirst, we define a new type MyId to serve as the \"keys\" of our\npartial maps.\n\nstructure MyId where\n  val : Nat\nstructure MyId where\n  val : Nat\nstructure MyId where\n  val : Nat\n\n\nInternally, a MyId is just a number.  Introducing a separate type\nby wrapping each Nat makes definitions more readable and gives us\nflexibility to change representations later if we want to.\n\n\n\nWe'll also need an equality test for MyIds:\n\ndef MyId.beq (x₁ x₂ : MyId) : Bool :=\n  x₁.val == x₂.val\ndef MyId.beq (x₁ x₂ : MyId) : Bool :=\n  x₁.val == x₂.val\ndef MyId.beq (x₁ x₂ : MyId) : Bool :=\n  x₁.val == x₂.val\n\n\ntheorem MyId.beq_refl (x : MyId) : MyId.beq x x = true := by\n  solution!\n    dsimp [beq]\n    rw [BEq.refl]\ntheorem MyId.beq_refl (x : MyId) : MyId.beq x x = true := by\n  sorry\ntheorem MyId.beq_refl (x : MyId) : MyId.beq x x = true := by\n  sorry\n\n\n\n\nNow we define the type of partial maps:\n\ninductive PartialMap : Type where\n  | empty : PartialMap\n  | record (i : MyId) (v : Nat) (m : PartialMap) : PartialMap\ninductive PartialMap : Type where\n  | empty : PartialMap\n  | record (i : MyId) (v : Nat) (m : PartialMap) : PartialMap\ninductive PartialMap : Type where\n  | empty : PartialMap\n  | record (i : MyId) (v : Nat) (m : PartialMap) : PartialMap\n\n\n\n\nnamespace PartialMap\nnamespace PartialMap\nnamespace PartialMap\n\n\n\n\nThe update function overrides the entry for a given key in a\npartial map by shadowing it with a new one (or simply adds a new\nentry if the given key is not already present).\n\ndef update (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (value : Nat) : PartialMap :=\n  record x value d\ndef update (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (value : Nat) : PartialMap :=\n  record x value d\ndef update (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (value : Nat) : PartialMap :=\n  record x value d\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe can define functions on PartialMaps by pattern matching.\n\ndef find (x : MyId) (d : PartialMap) : NatOption :=\n  match d with\n  | empty => .none\n  | record y v d' =>\n    bif MyId.beq x y then .some v\n    else find x d'\ndef find (x : MyId) (d : PartialMap) : NatOption :=\n  match d with\n  | empty => .none\n  | record y v d' =>\n    bif MyId.beq x y then .some v\n    else find x d'\ndef find (x : MyId) (d : PartialMap) : NatOption :=\n  match d with\n  | empty => .none\n  | record y v d' =>\n    bif MyId.beq x y then .some v\n    else find x d'\n\n\nIs the following claim true or false?theorem quiz1 (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (v : Nat) :\n    find x (update d x v) = .some v := by\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [MyId.beq_refl]\n  dsimp\ntheorem quiz1 (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (v : Nat) :\n    find x (update d x v) = .some v := by\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [MyId.beq_refl]\n  dsimp\ntheorem quiz1 (d : PartialMap) (x : MyId) (v : Nat) :\n    find x (update d x v) = .some v := by\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [MyId.beq_refl]\n  dsimp\n(A) True\n(B) False\n(C) Not sure\n\nIs the following claim true or false?theorem quiz2  (d : PartialMap) (x y : MyId) (o : Nat) :\n    MyId.beq x y = false →\n    find x (update d y o) = find x d := by\n  intro h\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [h]\n  dsimp\ntheorem quiz2  (d : PartialMap) (x y : MyId) (o : Nat) :\n    MyId.beq x y = false →\n    find x (update d y o) = find x d := by\n  intro h\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [h]\n  dsimp\ntheorem quiz2  (d : PartialMap) (x y : MyId) (o : Nat) :\n    MyId.beq x y = false →\n    find x (update d y o) = find x d := by\n  intro h\n  dsimp [update, find]\n  rw [h]\n  dsimp\n(A) True\n(B) False\n(C) Not sure\n\n\n\nend PartialMap\nend PartialMap\nend PartialMap\n\n\n\n\nend Lists\nend Lists\nend Lists\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Lists: Working with Structured Data","header":"5.5. Partial Maps","id":"/Lists/#Logical-Foundations--Lists___-Working-with-Structured-Data--Partial-Maps"}});